WEBVTT

00:00:00.129 --> 00:00:03.252
Pre-aggregation can help control grain.

00:00:03.252 --> 00:00:07.702
First summarize the fact table to the level you actually need.

00:00:07.702 --> 00:00:12.142
Then perform later joins or pivots from that stable grain.

00:00:12.142 --> 00:00:19.987
This separates fact aggregation from presentation reshaping and can make the query easier to verify.

00:00:19.987 --> 00:00:24.937
Joining detail tables before reshaping can multiply rows.

00:00:24.937 --> 00:00:32.522
If the target is one row per patient or product, summarize each one-to-many source to the target grain before

00:00:32.522 --> 00:00:40.320
combining them. This keeps measures interpretable and prevents a pivot from hiding earlier join inflation.
